{
  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Focus on independence process and state redesign (majority of SNP MPs triggers negotiations and a referendum; written constitution; abolish unelected influence and reform the monarchy; Scottish Defence Forces; remove Trident; phased withdrawal from NATO). Care/equality measures include NHS funding increases and prevention focus; ban tobacco advertising; increased child benefit and restored 16–17 benefits; substantial pensioner package (ending means‑testing for residential care, removing standing charges); free nursery education; restore student grants; build 20,000 affordable homes; adopt EU Social Chapter; minimum wage and trade union rights; law and order with ‘zero tolerance’. Economy features significant business tax cuts (corporation tax, small company rate, abolish Class IV NICs) alongside removing the NI ceiling for higher earners and cutting VAT on domestic fuel. TEXT_D: Strong care/equality agenda—£2bn/year extra for education; universal early years; NHS +£540m/year, recruit nurses/doctors, max 6‑month waits, free eye/dental checks; end rough sleeping by 2000; housing expansion and tenant rights; new Carer’s Benefit; national childcare strategy; Low Income Benefit simplifying support; raise personal allowance and a 50% rate over £100k; stronger anti‑discrimination and equal rights (women, disabled, minorities, LGBT; equal age of consent; repeal Section 28; outlaw age discrimination); restorative justice and victim support. Balanced authority/loyalty—3,000 more police; faster justice; Independent Bank of England; maintain defence capability, keep Trident (fewer warheads), support NATO; constitutional reforms (PR, Bill of Rights, FOI). Environment: 30% CO2 cut target, efficiency, renewables, pollution tax shift.",
  "reasoning": "Because the electorate’s top priorities are Care and Equality, TEXT_D aligns better by offering broad, concrete investments in health, education, housing, social protection, and equal rights while maintaining moderate deference to national and international institutions (police, NATO, Trident). TEXT_C devotes major emphasis to independence and constitutional change (loyalty/authority reordering) and mixes in large business‑tax cuts and NATO exit, which tilt it away from the profile’s strong care/equality focus and moderate authority/loyalty preferences.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_D"
}
